  "events": [
    {"id":"STR-01/E1","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":1,"role":"user","event_type":"issue_body","source":{"source_id":"gh:issue:495","kind":"issue","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":495,"database_id":"438578988","node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0Mzg1Nzg5ODg=","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/495","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2019-04-30T02:19:41Z","source_updated_at":"2023-06-01T18:57:30Z","actor":"yihuang","summary":"The report shows BaseHTTPMiddleware awaiting request.form() and the endpoint awaiting request.form() again, after which the request blocks.","source_content_sha256":"9c7736e9812922e6f6038f0a0954c2d82c88d9836ae6670c5782151d03db85bc"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E2","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":2,"role":"user","event_type":"issue_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:issue-comment:488205460","kind":"issue_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":495,"database_id":"488205460","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODIwNTQ2MA==","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/495#issuecomment-488205460","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2019-05-01T03:55:29Z","source_updated_at":"2019-05-01T04:19:25Z","actor":"blueyed","summary":"Source inspection confirms middleware and routing construct different Request paths over the receive channel, and asks for a Starlette regression test.","source_content_sha256":"499cb19835e0f4f526c4b90b40d045707009024db30fa89031c8b7266b800b62"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E3","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":3,"role":"user","event_type":"pull_request_body","source":{"source_id":"gh:pr:500","kind":"pull_request","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":500,"database_id":"275466541","node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0Mjc1NDY2NTQx","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/500","commit_sha":"d388e06d16db09931e424db6ba767317393da17b"},"occurred_at":"2019-05-02T18:15:50Z","source_updated_at":"2019-05-20T14:15:54Z","actor":"ricardomomm","summary":"PR 500 proposes caching body bytes in the ASGI scope so a newly constructed Request can read them, and its initial patch adds one repeated-Request test.","source_content_sha256":"2d60eb17002477ee519f9e96e3d82168771b66a2f647bcfdfd55e91a2f124223"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E4","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":4,"role":"user","event_type":"pull_request_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:pr-comment:494006150","kind":"pull_request_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":500,"database_id":"494006150","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5NDAwNjE1MA==","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/500#issuecomment-494006150","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2019-05-20T14:15:53Z","source_updated_at":"2019-05-20T14:15:53Z","actor":"lovelydinosaur","summary":"A maintainer punts the scope-cache patch because a broader design must define behavior when the request body is consumed as a stream; PR 500 closes unmerged at the same time.","source_content_sha256":"9193cd799ce494d0133e7f8a6a1f0294e91f4fa4ea9404414ca4bcb1dbb9122e"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E5","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":5,"role":"user","event_type":"issue_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:issue-comment:494008175","kind":"issue_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":495,"database_id":"494008175","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5NDAwODE3NQ==","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/495#issuecomment-494008175","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2019-05-20T14:20:46Z","source_updated_at":"2019-05-20T14:20:46Z","actor":"lovelydinosaur","summary":"The maintainer states the durable constraint: middleware body consumption should generally be avoided and streamed data can be irreversibly unavailable downstream.","source_content_sha256":"c542549559de27c3f1adfaf3b4e7ac862f2620685d4cd5c3c5679c1d6ae6229f"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E6","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":6,"role":"user","event_type":"issue_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:issue-comment:886876930","kind":"issue_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":495,"database_id":"886876930","node_id":"IC_kwDOCELT_M403KsC","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/495#issuecomment-886876930","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2021-07-26T17:08:46Z","source_updated_at":"2021-07-26T17:14:10Z","actor":"four43","summary":"Investigation distinguishes cached body/json reads from form(), which consumes the underlying stream and can raise Stream consumed; the supplied custom-route workaround is not a repository fix.","source_content_sha256":"026674190ddfa016cd9d9c1d5c9182a489ec21f045c0bb3640ad4ae2299358af"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E7","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":7,"role":"user","event_type":"issue_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:issue-comment:1101403203","kind":"issue_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":495,"database_id":"1101403203","node_id":"IC_kwDOCELT_M5BphRD","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/495#issuecomment-1101403203","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2022-04-18T13:19:37Z","source_updated_at":"2022-04-18T13:19:37Z","actor":"heyfavour","summary":"The receive channel is described as a queue: logging by consuming receive empties it, so the later request waits on an empty queue and blocks.","source_content_sha256":"aa53170cbb28d9f2298a12ed2e2f625341ff16e65f6f39b78e45b97badbcf1f4"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E8","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":8,"role":"user","event_type":"pull_request_body","source":{"source_id":"gh:pr:1692","kind":"pull_request","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":1692,"database_id":"967628660","node_id":"PR_kwDOCELT_M45rNd0","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/1692","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2022-06-15T03:13:28Z","source_updated_at":"2023-10-30T15:44:14Z","actor":"adriangb","summary":"PR 1692 opens as a new candidate in the request-stream lineage; its current body, final title, and current commit list are mutable outcome-era data and are not used to describe the creation-time implementation.","source_content_sha256":"09aaf24f68e660634770138b6d72973f600b896eb53ac1b6db64dd1b89018b89"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E9","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":9,"role":"user","event_type":"pull_request_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:pr-comment:1236394572","kind":"pull_request_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":1692,"database_id":"1236394572","node_id":"IC_kwDOCELT_M5JseJM","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/1692#issuecomment-1236394572","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2022-09-04T18:44:02Z","source_updated_at":"2022-09-04T18:51:53Z","actor":"adriangb","summary":"The proposal must preserve downstream receive replacements; tests for that behavior and client-disconnect handling are still explicit TODOs.","source_content_sha256":"bc75a09baf827f6b92ba2e590c29fd78538b8fad99a4676fb5d86eaf1b365c05"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E10","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":10,"role":"user","event_type":"issue_state","source":{"source_id":"gh:issue-event:7329871772","kind":"issue_state_event","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":1692,"database_id":"7329871772","node_id":"RTE_lADOCELT_M5LyzvtzwAAAAG05Pec","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/1692#event-7329871772","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2022-09-06T12:16:46Z","source_updated_at":null,"actor":"adriangb","summary":"After an intermediate downstream-ASGI title, the PR title narrows the proposed ownership boundary to reusing the body buffer specifically for call_next in BaseHTTPMiddleware.","source_content_sha256":"c995a11d6793d10334fe87f8d707614f50b8c40b07579bafa417b708d8a3f4f1"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E11","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":11,"role":"user","event_type":"pull_request_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:pr-comment:1265515733","kind":"pull_request_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":1692,"database_id":"1265515733","node_id":"IC_kwDOCELT_M5LbjzV","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/1692#issuecomment-1265515733","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2022-10-03T14:19:41Z","source_updated_at":"2022-10-03T14:19:41Z","actor":"adriangb","summary":"The author explicitly excludes endpoint-first consumption followed by middleware or exception-handler rereads; those require upstream information flow, though double consumption could fail instead of hanging.","source_content_sha256":"71e2f14bb33622396a0ba74d50fde03eed19eaeb7a96feb29d256f38c4d04196"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E12","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":12,"role":"user","event_type":"pull_request_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:pr-comment:1266401636","kind":"pull_request_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":1692,"database_id":"1266401636","node_id":"IC_kwDOCELT_M5Le8Fk","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/1692#issuecomment-1266401636","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2022-10-04T05:03:33Z","source_updated_at":"2022-10-04T05:03:33Z","actor":"adriangb","summary":"A before/after matrix shows the proposal fixes only middleware-first body consumption for the downstream endpoint, leaving endpoint-first and error-handler rereads unsupported; whether to land that narrow benefit remains open.","source_content_sha256":"fdf41537345dafc2af15d7547cccfdb1b7d8936fbd0cd599d12b406241fb8001"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E13","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":13,"role":"user","event_type":"issue_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:issue-comment:1522359931","kind":"issue_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":495,"database_id":"1522359931","node_id":"IC_kwDOCELT_M5avV57","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/495#issuecomment-1522359931","commit_sha":null},"occurred_at":"2023-04-25T20:15:26Z","source_updated_at":"2023-04-25T20:22:57Z","actor":"bricker","summary":"Four years later a user reports the same no-error hang, accepts full buffering as an explicit HMAC tradeoff, and explains that exhausting receive leaves Request waiting forever; the suggested scope/dummy-receive hacks are not production-ready.","source_content_sha256":"b6925423f26241c117964b0fa27485710ae07e8ac50d780bf9991eb25770e645"},
    {"id":"STR-01/E14","segment_id":"STR-01","ordinal":14,"role":"user","event_type":"pull_request_comment","source":{"source_id":"gh:pr-review-comment:1184692481","kind":"pull_request_comment","repository":"Kludex/starlette","number":1692,"database_id":"1184692481","node_id":"PRRC_kwDOCELT_M5GnPkB","url":"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/1692#discussion_r1184692481","commit_sha":"ec382274541720a688131053ec7247c4c5965f8d"},"occurred_at":"2023-05-04T08:19:59Z","source_updated_at":"2023-05-04T08:24:38Z","actor":"Kludex","summary":"Review challenges the stream state machine: more_body is not accounted for and a standalone Request receiving multiple chunks lacks coverage, so the current logic may mark consumption too early.","source_content_sha256":"c48a9f24616a2ddf6926ab8b2bcffa553ac5af738b9be327798511b8a4b3fe69"},
